#!/usr/bin/env jet
// The port-bar judge (#5072 c14, c34): whether each tool entry's Jet twin
// does its original's job at least as fast, and so may replace it.
//
//   jet Tools/gauntlet/PortBars.jet [--entry NAME] [--runs N] [--jet PATH] [--repo DIR]
//   jet Tools/gauntlet/PortBars.jet --measure [--entry NAME] [--repo DIR]
//
// `--measure` runs no case: it prints each side's tokens, branches, control
// nesting depth and files (with each file's tokens) under SOURCE RULES.
//
// Cases run in `port_bars_judge_<pid>_<ns>` under the scratch root
// ($JET_SCRATCH_ROOT, else $JET_STATE_ROOT, else Jet's user cache), never on
// a RAM-backed /tmp. A judge removes it when it ends, and on start removes the
// `port_bars_*` directories that killed judges left behind.
//
// A tool entry (Tools/gauntlet/entries/<name>/entry.json, "mode": "tool")
// names the original as `tool.original` and its Jet twin as `tool.jet`, with
// the fixtures and parity cases Tools/agent/ScriptPairing.jet describes. Each
// entry is judged against its own original only. Performance ranks first:
// the job, wall time and peak memory decide a switch, with the reasoning bar
// beside them; source tokens are measured and reported but block a switch
// only while a gap names no criterion.
//
// (1) parity: on every case both programs, each in a fresh copy of the
//     fixtures, exit with the case's `exit` (0 when it names none) and do the
//     same job. A case with a `check` (a Jet program in the entry) checks the
//     job: after each program the judge runs `jet CHECK STDOUT` in the case
//     directory, STDOUT being the file that holds what the program printed,
//     and the check must exit 0 and print the case's `expected` file byte for
//     byte; it prints the facts the job leaves (the files, commits and queue
//     lines it wrote, the facts its report states), never the program's
//     wording. A case without a check compares the program's own output with
//     `expected` byte for byte.
// (2) speed: N rounds (--runs, default 5) run every case once per side,
//     interleaved (the original first in even rounds, Jet first in odd
//     ones), after the parity runs have warmed both. A round's wall time is
//     the sum over its cases and its peak memory the largest peak resident
//     size of one case (GNU time's %M: ru_maxrss, the largest process; every
//     run goes through `time`, which must be on PATH). Jet wins a measure
//     only when every Jet round beats every original round;
//     when every original round beats every Jet round Jet loses; any overlap
//     is inconclusive, which fails the bar too. Jet must win both measures.
//     The report gives each measure's Jet/original ratio of medians.
// (3) reasoning: the entry's review record REVIEW_FILE scores both programs
//     on the fixed CHECKLIST and Jet's total is at least the original's, and
//     the measured proxies (branches, control nesting depth, and the
//     record's hand-written helpers a library call would replace) are no
//     worse for Jet. A missing record, a missing or unknown checklist item,
//     or an unknown field fails the bar; it never passes by default.
// (4) tokens: the Jet twin's source tokens against the original's, by one
//     written rule per language (TOKEN RULES below), always reported. Jet at
//     or below the original passes; a twin above it passes only when the
//     entry's `tool.token_gaps` names what closes the gap (each a Core API
//     criterion such as "#5072 c36" or a syntax ballot such as "D-SH-RUN1").
//
// The verdict is PASS only when all four bars hold. Every entry and every bar
// is judged and reported: one `entry<TAB>bar<TAB>PASS|FAIL<TAB>detail` row
// each, a `verdict` row per entry naming the bars it loses, then a summary.
// A lost bar's detail says by how much (the ratios, the token counts, the
// proxy deltas), so it can go onto a card as written. The exit is 0 when
// every judged entry passes, 1 when any fails, 64 when the judge cannot run.
// The repository keeps running an original until its entry passes here
// (AGENTS.md, Tooling in other languages); ScriptPairing.jet --check runs
// this judge on every entry a change switches over.
//
// TOKEN RULES. The `#!` line is not counted. Comments are not tokens: `//` to
// the line end in Jet and JavaScript, and `/* … */` in JavaScript; `#` to the
// line end in Python, and in shell where it starts a word. A string literal is
// one token: Jet "…" (with its `{…}` interpolations; `{{` is a brace) and
// """…"""; JavaScript '…', "…" and `…` (with its `${…}`); Python '…', "…",
// their tripled forms and an r, b, f or u prefix; shell '…', "…" and `…`. A
// shell `${…}` expansion is one token. A word is a run of letters, digits,
// `_` and non-ASCII bytes (a number may take one `.digits` part). Of the rest,
// each of MULTI_SYMBOLS is one token where it is written and every other byte
// is one token. A JavaScript regex literal is one token, as a pattern string
// is in the other languages. A `/` that starts no comment opens one where an
// operand is expected, by the token before it: at the start of the file; after
// one of REGEX_KEYWORDS (any other word ends an operand); after any symbol but
// `)`, `]`, `}` and a postfix `++` or `--`; after a `)` that closes the head of
// one of REGEX_HEADS; after a `}` that closes a block, not an object literal.
// A Jet program's `#Test(…) {…}` blocks are its proof, not
// its program: neither the tokens nor the proxies count them.
//
// SOURCE RULES. Both bars measure a program, not one file: the program's
// file, then every repository module it imports, transitively and once each,
// counted by the same rules. A module counts when its import names it
// relative to the importing file and it resolves to a file inside the
// repository: JavaScript `import … from './x.mjs'` (or '../…'); a shell
// `. "$(dirname "$0")/x.sh"` or `source` line; Python `from .x import …`;
// Jet `use name: "Module"` (`Module.jet` beside the file). A Jet package path
// dependency (`deps: { kit: ../kit, }` in the file's inline `package:` block)
// counts each file of the package's Source directory that declares a name the
// file's `use` lines take from it (`kit.[a, b]`, `kit.a`), then each file
// there declaring a word such a counted file uses; a counted package file
// reaches the path dependencies of its own package.jet the same way. Core,
// Node built-ins and installed packages are never counted.
//
// PROXY RULES. Branches are decisions, counted by one table per language that
// spells the same kinds of decision (DECISION TABLES); a decision written in a
// string literal (its interpolations too) or in a regex literal is data in
// every language and is not counted. Control nesting depth is the most
// control blocks open at once; function and type bodies are not control
// blocks. In Jet and JavaScript a `{` opens one when its line starts with one
// of CONTROL_WORDS or with `} else`, `} catch` or `} finally`, or when it
// follows `->` or `??`; in Python an indented block opens one when its header
// line starts with one of CONTROL_WORDS; in shell `if`, `for`, `while`,
// `until` and `case` open one and `fi`, `done` and `esac` close it.
//
// DECISION TABLES. Each kind of decision, as each language spells it; every
// listed spelling counts one, and a default (Jet `else`, JavaScript
// `default`, Python `case _`, shell `*)`) counts none in any language.
//
//   kind           Jet           JavaScript      Python          shell
//   condition      `if`          `if`, `?`       `if`, `elif`    `if`, `elif`
//   arm            each arm of   `case`          `case`          each case arm's
//                  `if {` or                                     `pattern)`
//                  `if x == {`
//   loop           `loop`        `for`, `while`  `for`, `while`  `for`, `while`,
//                                                                `until`
//   short circuit  `&&`, `||`    `&&`, `||`      `and`, `or`     `&&`, `||`
//   fallback       `??`          `??`, `?.`      `or`            `${x:-…}`, `${x-…}`,
//                                                                `${x:=…}`, `${x=…}`,
//                                                                `${x:+…}`, `${x+…}`,
//                                                                `${x:?…}`, `${x?…}`
//   handler        `??`          `catch`         `except`        `||`
//
// A Jet multi-arm `if` counts its arms in place of the `if`.
use {
    json: core.encoding.json
    files: core.files
    process: core.process
    sys: core.sys
    time: core.time
}

ENTRIES_ROOT: "Tools/gauntlet/entries"
// The review record, in the entry's directory.
REVIEW_FILE: "review.json"
DEFAULT_RUNS: 5
RUN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS: 600
OUTPUT_LIMIT: 268435456
BARS: [String]{"parity", "speed", "reasoning", "tokens"}
// The fixed reviewer checklist (#5072 c14), each item scored for each program
// 0 (no), 1 (partly) or 2 (yes): types visible at use, every failure path
// visible at the call, no hidden global or mutable state, data flows top to
// bottom, one obvious way per operation, and effects such as files, network
// and processes visible.
CHECKLIST: [String]{"types_visible_at_use", "failure_paths_visible_at_call", "no_hidden_global_or_mutable_state", "data_flows_top_to_bottom", "one_obvious_way_per_operation", "effects_visible"}
CHECKLIST_TOP: 2
// The fields of a review record; `helpers` (the hand-written helpers of each
// program a library call would replace, by name) may be left out.
REVIEW_FIELDS: [String]{"reviewer", "date", "checklist", "helpers"}
SIDES: [String]{"original", "jet"}
// The symbols of more than one byte, longest first.
MULTI_SYMBOLS: [String]{"===", "!==", "...", "..<", "&&", "||", "??", "?.", "->", "=>", "==", "!=", "<=", ">=", "::", "..", ";;", "<<", ">>", "+=", "-=", "*=", "/=", "|>"}
CONTROL_WORDS: [String]{"if", "else", "loop", "for", "while", "do", "switch", "try", "catch", "finally", "elif", "except", "with", "match", "case"}
// The JavaScript words after which a `/` opens a regex literal.
REGEX_KEYWORDS: [String]{"return", "typeof", "case", "do", "else", "in", "of", "new", "delete", "void", "throw", "instanceof", "yield", "await"}
// The JavaScript words whose `(…)` head ends where a statement begins.
REGEX_HEADS: [String]{"if", "while", "for", "with"}
// The JavaScript words after which a `{` opens a block.
BLOCK_WORDS: [String]{"else", "try", "finally", "do"}
// The symbols after which a JavaScript `{` opens a block.
BLOCK_SYMBOLS: [String]{")", ";", "{{", "}}", "=>"}
SHELL_OPENERS: [String]{"if", "for", "while", "until", "case"}
SHELL_CLOSERS: [String]{"fi", "done", "esac"}

#Error
JudgeError: struct {
    message: String
}

judge_fail: fn(message: String) -> JudgeError Never! { JudgeError{message: "port-bars: {message}"} }

Language: enum { Jet JavaScript Python Shell }

TokenKind: enum { Word Text Symbol }

// One source token: a word's or symbol's text ("" for a string literal);
// `first` marks the first token of its line and `column` the indentation
// before it then.
Token: struct {
    text: String
    kind: TokenKind
    first: Bool
    column: Int
}

// What the proxies measure of one program.
Proxies: struct {
    branches: Int
    depth: Int
}

EnvVar: struct {
    name: String
    value: String
}

// One case of an entry: what both programs run with and must give; `check`
// is the entry's Jet program that checks the job, or "".
Case: struct {
    args: [String]
    env: [EnvVar]
    exit: Int
    expected: String
    check: String
}

// A tool entry as the judge reads it; `problems` keep it from being judged.
Entry: struct {
    name: String
    dir: String
    original: String
    twin: String
    fixtures: String
    cases: [Case]
    // What closes the token gap: Core API criteria and syntax ballots.
    token_gaps: [String]
    problems: [String]
}

// One run of one program on one case; `problem` is why it did not run.
Run: struct {
    code: Int
    output: String
    errors: String
    wall_ns: Int
    peak_bytes: Int
    problem: String
}

// An entry's review record, read: the checklist totals and helper counts of
// both programs, and every problem that makes the record fail.
Review: struct {
    reviewer: String
    date: String
    original: Int
    jet: Int
    helpers_original: Int
    helpers_jet: Int
    problems: [String]
}

Bar: struct {
    name: String
    pass: Bool
    detail: String
}

Report: struct {
    entry: String
    bars: [Bar]
}

// Every original round beats every Jet round, the reverse, or neither.
Lead: enum { Win Loss Even }

// ---- entries ----

field: fn(tree: Dyn, name: String) -> Dyn Never! {
    if tree == .Object(entries) {
        loop entry in entries {
            if entry.key == name -> return entry.value.copy()
        }
    }
    Dyn.Null
}

text_field: fn(tree: Dyn, name: String) -> String Never! {
    if field(tree, name) == .Text(value) -> return value.copy()
    ""
}

is_object: fn(tree: Dyn) -> Bool Never! {
    if tree == .Object(entries) -> return entries.len() >= 0
    false
}

is_null: fn(tree: Dyn) -> Bool Never! {
    if tree == .Null -> return true
    false
}

// An integral JSON number, whether built as an Int or parsed as a lexeme.
int_of: fn(tree: Dyn) -> Int? Never! {
    if tree == .Int(number) -> return Val(number)
    if tree == .Number(lexeme) {
        number: Int.parse(lexeme) ?? return None
        return Val(number)
    }
    None
}

keys_of: fn(tree: Dyn) -> [String] Never! {
    out := [String]{}
    if tree == .Object(entries) {
        loop entry in entries -> out.push(entry.key.copy())
    }
    out
}

// The tool entry `name` under `repo`, with every problem that keeps it from
// being judged.
read_entry: fn(repo: String, name: String) -[FS]> Entry Never! {
    dir: "{ENTRIES_ROOT}/{name}"
    entry := Entry{name: name.copy(), dir: dir.copy(), original: "", twin: "", fixtures: "", cases: [Case]{}, token_gaps: [String]{}, problems: [String]{}}
    text: files.read(files.join(repo, "{dir}/entry.json")) ?? {
        entry.problems.push("`{dir}/entry.json` cannot be read: {err}")
        return entry
    }
    tree: json.parse(text) ?? {
        entry.problems.push("`{dir}/entry.json` is not JSON: {err}")
        return entry
    }
    if text_field(tree, "mode") != "tool" -> entry.problems.push("it is not a tool entry (\"mode\": \"tool\")")
    tool: field(tree, "tool")
    entry.original = text_field(tool, "original")
    entry.twin = text_field(tool, "jet")
    entry.fixtures = text_field(tool, "fixtures")
    if entry.original == "" || !files.is_file(files.join(repo, entry.original)) -> entry.problems.push("its original `{entry.original}` does not exist")
    if !entry.twin.ends_with(".jet") || !files.is_file(files.join(repo, entry.twin)) -> entry.problems.push("its Jet twin `{entry.twin}` does not exist")
    if entry.fixtures != "" && !files.is_dir(files.join(repo, "{dir}/{entry.fixtures}")) -> entry.problems.push("its fixtures `{dir}/{entry.fixtures}` are not a directory")
    if field(tool, "token_gaps") == .Array(gaps) {
        loop gap in gaps {
            named: if gap == .Text(written) -> written.copy() else -> ""
            if named.starts_with("D-") || (named.starts_with("#") && named.contains(" c")) -> entry.token_gaps.push(named) else -> entry.problems.push("its `tool.token_gaps` holds {json.dumps(gap) ?? "a value"}, not a criterion (\"#5072 c36\") or a ballot (\"D-SH-RUN1\")")
        }
    }
    listed: if field(tool, "cases") == .Array(items) -> items.copy() else -> [Dyn]{}
    if listed.len() == 0 -> entry.problems.push("it has no `tool.cases`")
    loop index in 0..<listed.len() {
        item: listed[index]
        args := [String]{}
        if field(item, "args") == .Array(values) {
            loop value in values {
                if value == .Text(word) {
                    args.push(word.copy())
                } else {
                    entry.problems.push("case {index + 1} has an `args` value that is not a string")
                }
            }
        }
        env := [EnvVar]{}
        if field(item, "env") == .Object(pairs) {
            loop pair in pairs {
                if pair.value == .Text(value) {
                    env.push(EnvVar{name: pair.key.copy(), value: value.copy()})
                } else {
                    entry.problems.push("case {index + 1}'s variable `{pair.key}` is not a string")
                }
            }
        }
        exit_value: field(item, "exit")
        code: int_of(exit_value) ?? 0
        if !is_null(exit_value) && int_of(exit_value) == None -> entry.problems.push("case {index + 1}'s `exit` is not an integer")
        expected: text_field(item, "expected")
        if expected == "" || !files.is_file(files.join(repo, "{dir}/{expected}")) -> entry.problems.push("case {index + 1}'s expected output `{dir}/{expected}` does not exist")
        check: text_field(item, "check")
        if check != "" && (!check.ends_with(".jet") || !files.is_file(files.join(repo, "{dir}/{check}"))) -> entry.problems.push("case {index + 1}'s check `{dir}/{check}` is not a Jet program")
        entry.cases.push(Case{args: args, env: env, exit: code, expected: expected, check: check})
    }
    entry
}

// The names of the tool entries under `repo`, in name order.
tool_entries: fn(repo: String) -[FS]> [String] JudgeError! {
    root: files.join(repo, ENTRIES_ROOT)
    listed: files.list_dir(root) ?? return Err(judge_fail("`{root}` cannot be listed: {err}"))
    names := [String]{}
    loop item in listed {
        if !item.is_dir -> next
        text: files.read(files.join(root, "{item.name}/entry.json")) ?? next
        tree: json.parse(text) ?? next
        if text_field(tree, "mode") == "tool" -> names.push(item.name.copy())
    }
    names.sort()
    Ok(names)
}

// ---- runs ----

// The command that runs the original at `path`: the interpreter its
// extension names, else the file itself through its `#!` line, as the
// gauntlet harness runs it.
original_command: fn(path: String) -> [String] Never! {
    if path.ends_with(".mjs") || path.ends_with(".js") || path.ends_with(".cjs") || path.ends_with(".ts") -> return [String]{"node", path.copy()}
    if path.ends_with(".py") -> return [String]{"python3", path.copy()}
    if path.ends_with(".sh") || path.ends_with(".bash") -> return [String]{"bash", path.copy()}
    [String]{path.copy()}
}

// The variables every run gets: a `jet` given as a path goes first on PATH
// and is $JET, which the scripts run.
jet_env: fn(jet: String) -[Env]> [EnvVar] Never! {
    out := [EnvVar]{}
    if !jet.contains("/") -> return out
    path: process.env_get("PATH") ?? ""
    out.push(EnvVar{name: "PATH", value: "{files.dirname(jet)}:{path}"})
    out.push(EnvVar{name: "JET", value: jet.copy()})
    out
}

not_run: fn(problem: String) -> Run Never! { Run{code: -1, output: "", errors: "", wall_ns: 0, peak_bytes: 0, problem: problem.copy()} }

// Runs `argv` with `case`'s arguments and variables at `cwd`, a fresh copy
// of `fixtures` (an empty directory when it is ""), under GNU `time` at
// `timer` for its peak memory: a program the judge starts itself inherits the
// judge's own high-water mark in ru_maxrss, one `time` starts does not.
run_case: fn(argv: [String], case: Case, inherited: [EnvVar], fixtures: String, cwd: String, timer: String) -[Env, Exec, FS, Time, Time.Wait]> Run Never! {
    files.remove_all(cwd) ?? ()
    files.create_dir_all(cwd) ?? return not_run("`{cwd}` cannot be made: {err}")
    if fixtures != "" {
        // `cp -a` keeps a symbolic link as it is, so a relative one still
        // points inside the copy.
        copied: process.cmd([String]{"cp", "-a", "{fixtures}/.", cwd.copy()}).run() ?? return not_run("cp cannot start: {err}")
        if copied.code != 0 -> return not_run("the fixtures cannot be copied: {copied.errors.trim()}")
    }
    stats: "{cwd}.peak"
    command := [String]{timer.copy(), "-f", "%M", "-o", stats.copy(), "--"}
    command.extend(argv.copy())
    command.extend(case.args.copy())
    spec := process.cmd(command).cwd(cwd).timeout(time.duration_seconds(RUN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS)).output_limit(OUTPUT_LIMIT)
    loop setting in inherited -> spec = spec.env(setting.name, setting.value)
    loop setting in case.env -> spec = spec.env(setting.name, setting.value)
    watch: time.instant()
    receipt: spec.run() ?? return not_run("`{timer}` cannot start: {err}")
    wall: watch.elapsed().ns
    code := receipt.code
    if receipt.signal == .Val(number) -> code = 128 + number
    if receipt.timed_out -> code = 124
    // The last line is the peak in KiB; one before it may say how the
    // program exited.
    peak_kib := 0
    loop line in (files.read(stats) ?? "").lines() {
        if line.trim() != "" -> peak_kib = Int.parse(line.trim()) ?? 0
    }
    files.remove_all(stats) ?? ()
    Run{code: code, output: receipt.output.copy(), errors: receipt.errors.copy(), wall_ns: wall, peak_bytes: peak_kib * 1024, problem: ""}
}

// `run` with the facts its job left in `cwd` as its output: what the case's
// check, the entry's Jet program at `check`, prints when `jet` runs it in
// `cwd` with the path of a file holding the program's own output.
checked: fn(run: Run, check: String, jet: String, case: Case, inherited: [EnvVar], cwd: String) -> Run {
    if run.problem != "" -> return run.copy()
    printed: "{cwd}.stdout"
    files.write(printed, run.output) ?? return not_run("the program's output cannot be kept: {err}")
    spec := process.cmd([jet, check, printed]).cwd(cwd).timeout(time.duration_seconds(RUN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS)).output_limit(OUTPUT_LIMIT)
    loop setting in inherited.concat(case.env) -> spec = spec.env(setting.name, setting.value)
    receipt: spec.run() ?? return not_run("its check cannot start: {err}")
    files.remove(printed) ?? ()
    if receipt.code != 0 || receipt.signal != None || receipt.timed_out -> return not_run("its check `{case.check}` fails (exit {receipt.code}): {shown(near(receipt.errors.trim().bytes(), 0))}")
    Run{code: run.code, output: receipt.output, errors: run.errors, wall_ns: run.wall_ns, peak_bytes: run.peak_bytes, problem: ""}
}

// `text` quoted on one line.
shown: fn(text: String) -> String Never! { "\"{text.replace("\\", "\\\\").replace("\n", "\\n").replace("\t", "\\t")}\"" }

// At most 40 bytes of `bytes` from `at`.
near: fn(bytes: [U8], at: Int) -> String Never! {
    end: if at + 40 < bytes.len() -> at + 40 else -> bytes.len()
    String.from_bytes_lossy(bytes[at..<end])
}

// Where `actual` first differs from `expected`, or "" when they are equal.
mismatch: fn(expected: String, actual: String) -> String Never! {
    want: expected.bytes()
    got: actual.bytes()
    limit: if want.len() < got.len() -> want.len() else -> got.len()
    at := 0
    loop {
        if at >= limit || want[at] != got[at] -> break
        at += 1
    }
    if at == want.len() && at == got.len() -> return ""
    "byte {at}: expected {shown(near(want, at))}, got {shown(near(got, at))} (length {want.len()}/{got.len()})"
}

// Why one run failed its case, or "" when it passed.
run_failure: fn(run: Run, case: Case, expected: String) -> String Never! {
    if run.problem != "" -> return run.problem.copy()
    if run.code != case.exit -> return "exit {run.code}, not {case.exit}: {shown(near(run.errors.trim().bytes(), 0))}"
    mismatch(expected, run.output)
}

// ---- tokens ----

byte_at: fn(bytes: [U8], at: Int) -> Int Never! {
    if at < 0 || at >= bytes.len() -> return -1
    Int.from_u8(bytes[at])
}

is_digit: fn(code: Int) -> Bool Never! { code >= 48 && code <= 57 }

is_word_byte: fn(code: Int) -> Bool Never! { is_digit(code) || (code >= 65 && code <= 90) || (code >= 97 && code <= 122) || code == 95 || code >= 128 }

is_quote: fn(language: Language, code: Int) -> Bool Never! {
    if language == {
        .Jet -> code == 34
        .Python -> code == 34 || code == 39
        .JavaScript -> code == 34 || code == 39 || code == 96
        .Shell -> code == 34 || code == 39 || code == 96
    }
}

// The index just past the string literal that opens at `at`.
string_end: fn(bytes: [U8], at: Int, language: Language) -> Int Never! {
    quote: byte_at(bytes, at)
    if (language == .Python || language == .Jet) && byte_at(bytes, at + 1) == quote && byte_at(bytes, at + 2) == quote {
        inner := at + 3
        loop {
            if inner >= bytes.len() -> return bytes.len()
            if byte_at(bytes, inner) == 92 {
                inner += 2
                next
            }
            if byte_at(bytes, inner) == quote && byte_at(bytes, inner + 1) == quote && byte_at(bytes, inner + 2) == quote -> return inner + 3
            inner += 1
        }
    }
    raw: language == .Shell && quote == 39
    line_bound: language == .Jet || language == .Python || (language == .JavaScript && quote != 96)
    index := at + 1
    loop {
        if index >= bytes.len() -> return bytes.len()
        code: byte_at(bytes, index)
        if code == 92 && !raw {
            index += 2
            next
        }
        if code == quote -> return index + 1
        if code == 10 && line_bound -> return index
        if language == .Jet && code == 123 {
            if byte_at(bytes, index + 1) == 123 {
                index += 2
                next
            }
            index = braces_end(bytes, index + 1, language)
            next
        }
        if language == .JavaScript && quote == 96 && code == 36 && byte_at(bytes, index + 1) == 123 {
            index = braces_end(bytes, index + 2, language)
            next
        }
        index += 1
    }
}

// The index just past the `}` that closes a `{` written before `at`,
// stepping over the string literals inside.
braces_end: fn(bytes: [U8], at: Int, language: Language) -> Int Never! {
    depth := 0
    index := at
    loop {
        if index >= bytes.len() -> return bytes.len()
        code: byte_at(bytes, index)
        if is_quote(language, code) {
            index = string_end(bytes, index, language)
            next
        }
        if code == 123 -> depth += 1
        if code == 125 {
            if depth == 0 -> return index + 1
            depth -= 1
        }
        index += 1
    }
}

// 1 when a line comment starts at `at`, 2 for a JavaScript block comment,
// else 0.
comment_at: fn(bytes: [U8], at: Int, language: Language) -> Int Never! {
    code: byte_at(bytes, at)
    if language == .Jet || language == .JavaScript {
        if code == 47 && byte_at(bytes, at + 1) == 47 -> return 1
        if language == .JavaScript && code == 47 && byte_at(bytes, at + 1) == 42 -> return 2
        return 0
    }
    if code != 35 -> return 0
    if language == .Python -> return 1
    before: byte_at(bytes, at - 1)
    if before == -1 || before == 32 || before == 9 || before == 10 || before == 59 -> return 1
    0
}

// Whether bytes `start..<end` are a Python string prefix.
string_prefix: fn(bytes: [U8], start: Int, end: Int) -> Bool Never! {
    allowed: "rRbBfFuU".bytes()
    loop index in start..<end {
        if !allowed.contains(bytes[index]) -> return false
    }
    true
}

// The width of the symbol at `at`: one of MULTI_SYMBOLS, else one byte.
symbol_len: fn(bytes: [U8], at: Int) -> Int Never! {
    loop symbol in MULTI_SYMBOLS {
        spelled: symbol.bytes()
        if at + spelled.len() > bytes.len() -> next
        matched := true
        loop index in 0..<spelled.len() {
            if bytes[at + index] != spelled[index] {
                matched = false
                break
            }
        }
        if matched -> return spelled.len()
    }
    1
}

// The index of the line end at or after `at`.
line_end: fn(bytes: [U8], at: Int) -> Int Never! {
    index := at
    loop {
        if index >= bytes.len() || byte_at(bytes, index) == 10 -> return index
        index += 1
    }
}

// The index just past the `{…}` block at or after `at`, stepping over a
// `(…)` before it.
block_end: fn(list: [Token], at: Int) -> Int Never! {
    depth := 0
    index := at
    loop {
        if index >= list.len() -> return index
        token: list[index]
        if token.kind == .Symbol {
            if token.text == "(" || token.text == "[" || token.text == "{{" -> depth += 1
            if token.text == ")" || token.text == "]" -> depth -= 1
            if token.text == "}}" {
                depth -= 1
                if depth == 0 -> return index + 1
            }
        }
        index += 1
    }
}

// The Jet tokens `list` without its `#Test` blocks.
without_tests: fn(list: [Token]) -> [Token] Never! {
    out := [Token]{}
    index := 0
    loop {
        if index >= list.len() -> return out
        token: list[index]
        if token.kind == .Symbol && token.text == "#" && index + 1 < list.len() && list[index + 1].kind == .Word && list[index + 1].text == "Test" {
            index = block_end(list, index + 2)
            next
        }
        out.push(token.copy())
        index += 1
    }
}

// The index of the `open` symbol that the `close` symbol at `at` in `list`
// closes, or -1.
opener_of: fn(list: [Token], at: Int, open: String, close: String) -> Int Never! {
    depth := 0
    index := at
    loop index >= 0 {
        token: list[index]
        if token.kind == .Symbol && token.text == close -> depth += 1
        if token.kind == .Symbol && token.text == open {
            depth -= 1
            if depth == 0 -> return index
        }
        index -= 1
    }
    -1
}

// Whether the JavaScript token at `at` in `list` ends an operand: a literal,
// a word but REGEX_KEYWORDS, `)` or `]`.
operand_ends: fn(list: [Token], at: Int) -> Bool Never! {
    if at < 0 -> return false
    token: list[at]
    if token.kind == {
        .Text -> true
        .Word -> !REGEX_KEYWORDS.contains(token.text)
        .Symbol -> token.text == ")" || token.text == "]"
    }
}

// Whether the JavaScript `(` at `open` in `list` opens the head of one of
// REGEX_HEADS (`for await (` too).
control_head: fn(list: [Token], open: Int) -> Bool Never! {
    if open < 1 || list[open - 1].kind != .Word -> return false
    word: list[open - 1].text
    if word == "await" -> return open >= 2 && list[open - 2].text == "for"
    REGEX_HEADS.contains(word)
}

// Whether the JavaScript `{` at `open` in `list` opens a block, not an
// object literal: at the start of a statement or after BLOCK_WORDS or
// BLOCK_SYMBOLS.
block_brace: fn(list: [Token], open: Int) -> Bool Never! {
    if open < 0 -> return false
    if open == 0 -> return true
    before: list[open - 1]
    if before.kind == {
        .Text -> false
        .Word -> BLOCK_WORDS.contains(before.text)
        .Symbol -> BLOCK_SYMBOLS.contains(before.text)
    }
}

// Whether a JavaScript `/` after the tokens `list` opens a regex literal
// (TOKEN RULES): where an operand is expected, by the token before it.
regex_opens: fn(list: [Token]) -> Bool Never! {
    at: list.len() - 1
    if at < 0 -> return true
    last: list[at]
    if last.kind == .Text -> return false
    if last.kind == .Word -> return REGEX_KEYWORDS.contains(last.text)
    // `++` and `--` are two symbols: postfix after an operand, else prefix.
    if (last.text == "+" || last.text == "-") && at >= 1 && list[at - 1].kind == .Symbol && list[at - 1].text == last.text -> return !operand_ends(list, at - 2)
    if last.text == ")" -> return control_head(list, opener_of(list, at, "(", ")"))
    if last.text == "}}" -> return block_brace(list, opener_of(list, at, "{{", "}}"))
    last.text != "]"
}

// The index just past the JavaScript regex literal that opens at `at`, its
// flags too; an unclosed one ends at its line end.
regex_end: fn(bytes: [U8], at: Int) -> Int Never! {
    in_class := false
    index := at + 1
    loop {
        code: byte_at(bytes, index)
        if code == -1 || code == 10 -> return index
        if code == 92 {
            index += 2
            next
        }
        if code == 47 && !in_class {
            index += 1
            loop is_word_byte(byte_at(bytes, index)) {
                index += 1
            }
            return index
        }
        if code == 91 -> in_class = true
        if code == 93 -> in_class = false
        index += 1
    }
}

// The tokens of `source` by `language`'s rule (TOKEN RULES).
tokens: fn(source: String, language: Language) -> [Token] Never! {
    bytes: source.bytes()
    out := [Token]{}
    at := 0
    if byte_at(bytes, 0) == 35 && byte_at(bytes, 1) == 33 -> at = line_end(bytes, 0)
    first := true
    column := 0
    loop {
        if at >= bytes.len() -> return out
        code: byte_at(bytes, at)
        if code == 10 {
            at += 1
            first = true
            column = 0
            next
        }
        if code == 92 && byte_at(bytes, at + 1) == 10 && (language == .Shell || language == .Python) {
            at += 2
            next
        }
        if code == 32 || code == 9 || code == 13 {
            if first -> column += 1
            at += 1
            next
        }
        comment: comment_at(bytes, at, language)
        if comment == 1 {
            at = line_end(bytes, at)
            next
        }
        if comment == 2 {
            at += 2
            loop {
                if at >= bytes.len() -> break
                if byte_at(bytes, at) == 42 && byte_at(bytes, at + 1) == 47 {
                    at += 2
                    break
                }
                at += 1
            }
            next
        }
        start: at
        kind := TokenKind.Symbol
        if is_quote(language, code) {
            at = string_end(bytes, at, language)
            kind = .Text
        } else if language == .JavaScript && code == 47 && regex_opens(out) {
            at = regex_end(bytes, at)
            kind = .Text
        } else if language == .Shell && code == 36 && byte_at(bytes, at + 1) == 123 {
            at = braces_end(bytes, at + 2, language)
            kind = .Word
        } else if is_word_byte(code) {
            at += 1
            loop {
                if !is_word_byte(byte_at(bytes, at)) -> break
                at += 1
            }
            if is_digit(code) && byte_at(bytes, at) == 46 && is_digit(byte_at(bytes, at + 1)) {
                at += 1
                loop {
                    if !is_digit(byte_at(bytes, at)) -> break
                    at += 1
                }
            }
            kind = .Word
            if language == .Python && at - start <= 2 && is_quote(language, byte_at(bytes, at)) && string_prefix(bytes, start, at) {
                at = string_end(bytes, at, language)
                kind = .Text
            }
        } else {
            at += symbol_len(bytes, at)
        }
        text: if kind == .Text -> "" else -> String.from_bytes_lossy(bytes[start..<at])
        out.push(Token{text: text, kind: kind, first: first, column: column})
        first = false
    }
}

// The language of a program at `path` whose first line is `first_line`:
// by extension, else by its `#!` interpreter.
language_of: fn(path: String, first_line: String) -> Language? Never! {
    if path.ends_with(".jet") -> return Val(Language.Jet)
    if path.ends_with(".mjs") || path.ends_with(".js") || path.ends_with(".cjs") || path.ends_with(".ts") -> return Val(Language.JavaScript)
    if path.ends_with(".py") -> return Val(Language.Python)
    if path.ends_with(".sh") || path.ends_with(".bash") -> return Val(Language.Shell)
    if !first_line.starts_with("#!") -> return None
    words := [String]{}
    loop word in first_line.slice(2, first_line.len()).trim().split(" ").to_list() {
        if word.trim() != "" && !word.starts_with("-") && !word.contains("=") -> words.push(word.trim().rpartition("/").tail.copy())
    }
    if words.len() == 0 -> return None
    interpreter: if words[0] == "env" && words.len() > 1 -> words[1].copy() else -> words[0].copy()
    if interpreter == "node" -> return Val(Language.JavaScript)
    if interpreter.starts_with("python") -> return Val(Language.Python)
    if interpreter == "sh" || interpreter == "bash" || interpreter == "dash" -> return Val(Language.Shell)
    if interpreter == "jet" -> return Val(Language.Jet)
    None
}

// ---- sources ----

// A program as the token and proxy bars measure it (SOURCE RULES): its file,
// then each repository module it imports, transitively and once each, with
// the token count of each file.
Program: struct {
    paths: [String]
    counts: [Int]
    tokens: [Token]
}

// `path` with its `.` and `..` segments resolved, or "" when it climbs out of
// the repository.
normalized: fn(path: String) -> String Never! {
    parts := [String]{}
    loop part in path.split("/").to_list() {
        if part == "" || part == "." -> next
        if part == ".." {
            if parts.len() == 0 -> return ""
            _ := parts.pop()
            next
        }
        parts.push(part.copy())
    }
    parts.join("/")
}

// The text inside the quotes `text` starts with, or "".
quoted: fn(text: String) -> String Never! {
    quote: if {
        text.starts_with("'") -> "'"
        text.starts_with("\"") -> "\""
        else -> return ""
    }
    text.removeprefix(quote).partition(quote).head.copy()
}

// The modules a Python `from .module import …` line imports, as paths
// relative to its file, joined by "\n"; "" for any other line.
python_import: fn(line: String) -> String Never! {
    if !line.starts_with("from .") || !line.contains(" import ") -> return ""
    split: line.removeprefix("from ").partition(" import ")
    rest := split.head.trim()
    dots := 0
    loop rest.starts_with(".") {
        rest = rest.removeprefix(".")
        dots += 1
    }
    up: "../".repeat(dots - 1)
    if rest != "" -> return "{up}{rest.replace(".", "/")}.py"
    names := [String]{}
    loop name in split.tail.split(",").to_list() -> names.push("{up}{name.trim()}.py")
    names.join("\n")
}

// The repository modules `text` imports, as written relative to its file.
imports_of: fn(text: String, language: Language) -> [String] Never! {
    out := [String]{}
    in_use_block := false
    loop raw in text.split("\n").to_list() {
        line: raw.trim()
        spec: if language == {
            .JavaScript -> {
                written: if {
                    !(line.starts_with("import") || line.starts_with("export") || line.starts_with("}}")) -> ""
                    line.contains(" from ") -> quoted(line.partition(" from ").tail.trim())
                    else -> quoted(line.removeprefix("import").trim())
                }
                if written.starts_with("./") || written.starts_with("../") -> written else -> ""
            }
            .Shell -> {
                word: if line.starts_with(". ") || line.starts_with("source ") -> line.partition(" ").tail.trim().replace("\"", "").replace("'", "") else -> ""
                if {
                    word.starts_with("$(dirname $0)/") -> word.removeprefix("$(dirname $0)/")
                    word.starts_with("$(dirname ${{BASH_SOURCE[0]}})/") -> word.removeprefix("$(dirname ${{BASH_SOURCE[0]}})/")
                    else -> ""
                }
            }
            .Python -> python_import(line)
            .Jet -> {
                if line == "use {{" -> in_use_block = true
                if in_use_block && line == "}}" -> in_use_block = false
                named: if {
                    in_use_block || line.starts_with("use ") -> quoted(line.partition(":").tail.trim())
                    else -> ""
                }
                if named == "" || named.ends_with(".jet") -> named else -> "{named}.jet"
            }
        }
        if spec != "" -> out.push(spec)
    }
    out
}

// The path dependencies of a Jet file's inline `package:` block, each
// "name\tpath" with the path as written relative to the file.
package_deps: fn(text: String) -> [String] Never! {
    out := [String]{}
    in_deps := false
    loop raw in text.split("\n").to_list() {
        line: raw.trim()
        if line == "deps: {{" {
            in_deps = true
            next
        }
        if !in_deps -> next
        if line.starts_with("}}") -> return out
        pair: line.removesuffix(",").partition(":")
        written: pair.tail.trim()
        path: if written.starts_with("\"") -> quoted(written) else -> written
        if path != "" -> out.push("{pair.head.trim()}\t{path}")
    }
    out
}

// The names a Jet file's `use` lines take from package `name`: each of
// `name.[a, b]`, and `a` of `name.a`.
package_names: fn(text: String, name: String) -> [String] Never! {
    out := [String]{}
    prefix: "{name}."
    in_use_block := false
    loop raw in text.split("\n").to_list() {
        line: raw.trim()
        if line == "use {{" {
            in_use_block = true
            next
        }
        if in_use_block && line == "}}" -> in_use_block = false
        if !in_use_block && !line.starts_with("use ") -> next
        bare: line.removeprefix("use ").trim()
        target: if bare.starts_with(prefix) -> bare else -> bare.partition(":").tail.trim()
        if !target.starts_with(prefix) -> next
        rest: target.removeprefix(prefix)
        if !rest.starts_with("[") {
            out.push(rest.partition(".").head.trim())
            next
        }
        loop word in rest.removeprefix("[").partition("]").head.split(",").to_list() {
            if word.trim() != "" -> out.push(word.trim())
        }
    }
    out
}

// The top-level names a Jet source declares: each line that starts with a
// word directly followed by `:`.
declared: fn(text: String) -> [String] Never! {
    out := [String]{}
    loop line in text.split("\n").to_list() {
        if !line.contains(":") -> next
        name: line.partition(":").head
        bytes: name.bytes()
        word := bytes.len() > 0
        loop byte in bytes {
            if !is_word_byte(Int.from_u8(byte)) -> word = false
        }
        if word -> out.push(name.copy())
    }
    out
}

// The files of the package at `dir`'s Source directory that declare one of
// `wanted`, in name order.
package_sources: fn(repo: String, dir: String, wanted: [String]) -[FS]> [String] Never! {
    source: "{dir}/Source"
    listed: files.list_dir(files.join(repo, source)) ?? return [String]{}
    out := [String]{}
    loop item in listed {
        if item.is_dir || !item.name.ends_with(".jet") -> next
        path: "{source}/{item.name}"
        text: files.read(files.join(repo, path)) ?? next
        hit := false
        loop name in declared(text) {
            if wanted.contains(name) -> hit = true
        }
        if hit -> out.push(path)
    }
    out.sort()
    out
}

// The program at `path` in `repo`, written in `language`.
program: fn(repo: String, path: String, language: Language) -[FS]> Program Never! {
    found := Program{paths: [String]{path.copy()}, counts: [Int]{}, tokens: [Token]{}}
    // The package directory each path belongs to, "" for none.
    owners := [String]{""}
    index := 0
    loop index < found.paths.len() {
        file: found.paths[index].copy()
        text: files.read(files.join(repo, file)) ?? ""
        listed: tokens(text, language)
        counted: if language == .Jet -> without_tests(listed) else -> listed
        words := [String]{}
        loop at in 0..<counted.len() {
            if counted[at].kind == .Word -> words.push(counted[at].text.copy())
        }
        found.counts.push(counted.len())
        found.tokens.extend(counted)
        loop written in imports_of(text, language) {
            loop spec in written.split("\n").to_list() {
                target: normalized("{files.dirname(file)}/{spec}")
                if target != "" && !found.paths.contains(target) && files.is_file(files.join(repo, target)) {
                    found.paths.push(target)
                    owners.push("")
                }
            }
        }
        if language == .Jet {
            reached := [String]{}
            owner: owners[index].copy()
            if owner != "" {
                loop target in package_sources(repo, owner, words) -> reached.push("{owner}\t{target}")
                manifest: files.read(files.join(repo, "{owner}/package.jet")) ?? ""
                loop dep in package_deps(manifest) {
                    pair: dep.partition("\t")
                    dir: normalized("{owner}/{pair.tail}")
                    if dir == "" -> next
                    loop target in package_sources(repo, dir, package_names(text, pair.head)) -> reached.push("{dir}\t{target}")
                }
            }
            loop dep in package_deps(text) {
                pair: dep.partition("\t")
                dir: normalized("{files.dirname(file)}/{pair.tail}")
                if dir == "" -> next
                loop target in package_sources(repo, dir, package_names(text, pair.head)) -> reached.push("{dir}\t{target}")
            }
            loop pair in reached {
                split: pair.partition("\t")
                if !found.paths.contains(split.tail) {
                    found.paths.push(split.tail.copy())
                    owners.push(split.head.copy())
                }
            }
        }
        index += 1
    }
    found
}

// Each file of `found` with its token count.
program_files: fn(found: Program) -> String Never! {
    parts := [String]{}
    loop index in 0..<found.paths.len() -> parts.push("{found.paths[index]} {found.counts[index]}")
    parts.join(", ")
}

// ---- proxies ----

// The DECISION TABLES spellings of `language` that count one where they are
// written; `ruled_branches` and `shell_arms` count the rest.
branch_words: fn(language: Language) -> [String] Never! {
    if language == {
        .Jet -> [String]{"loop", "&&", "||", "??"}
        .JavaScript -> [String]{"if", "for", "while", "case", "catch", "&&", "||", "??", "?", "?."}
        .Python -> [String]{"if", "elif", "for", "while", "except", "and", "or"}
        .Shell -> [String]{"if", "elif", "for", "while", "until", "&&", "||"}
    }
}

// The decisions the DECISION TABLES count by rule at token `index`: a Jet
// `if` (its arms when multi-arm), a Python `case` but `case _`, and the
// fallbacks of a shell `${…}` expansion.
ruled_branches: fn(list: [Token], index: Int, language: Language) -> Int Never! {
    token: list[index]
    if token.kind != .Word -> return 0
    if language == {
        .Jet -> if token.text == "if" -> jet_if_branches(list, index) else -> 0
        .JavaScript -> 0
        .Python -> if token.text == "case" && !python_default(list, index) -> 1 else -> 0
        .Shell -> shell_fallbacks(token.text)
    }
}

// Whether the Python `case` at `at` is the default `case _:`.
python_default: fn(list: [Token], at: Int) -> Bool Never! {
    at + 2 < list.len() && list[at + 1].text == "_" && list[at + 2].text == ":"
}

// Whether `code` is one of the shell's one-byte special parameters.
is_shell_special: fn(code: Int) -> Bool Never! {
    code == 64 || code == 42 || code == 35 || code == 63 || code == 36 || code == 33 || code == 45
}

// The fallbacks in the shell `${…}` expansion `text`, nested ones too: each
// `${name` followed by `-`, `=`, `+` or `?`, with or without a `:`.
shell_fallbacks: fn(text: String) -> Int Never! {
    bytes: text.bytes()
    count := 0
    loop at in 0..<bytes.len() {
        if byte_at(bytes, at) != 36 || byte_at(bytes, at + 1) != 123 -> next
        index := at + 2
        loop is_word_byte(byte_at(bytes, index)) {
            index += 1
        }
        if index == at + 2 && is_shell_special(byte_at(bytes, index)) -> index += 1
        if byte_at(bytes, index) == 58 -> index += 1
        operator: byte_at(bytes, index)
        if operator == 45 || operator == 61 || operator == 43 || operator == 63 -> count += 1
    }
    count
}

// Where a shell `case` block stands: before its `in`, in an arm's pattern,
// or in an arm's commands.
CaseState: enum { Header Pattern Body }

// The arms of the shell `case` blocks in `list` but the default `*)`: each
// arm's `pattern)`, after its block's `in` or the terminator before it, one of
// `;;`, `;&` and `;;&` (the symbols `;;`, or `;` or `;;` then `&`).
shell_arms: fn(list: [Token]) -> Int Never! {
    states := [CaseState]{}
    pattern := ""
    arms := 0
    loop index in 0..<list.len() {
        token: list[index]
        word: token.kind == .Word
        symbol: token.kind == .Symbol
        before: if index > 0 && list[index - 1].kind == .Symbol -> list[index - 1].text else -> ""
        if word && token.text == "case" {
            states.push(.Header)
            next
        }
        if states.len() == 0 -> next
        last: states.len() - 1
        if word && token.text == "esac" {
            _ := states.pop()
            pattern = ""
            next
        }
        if states[last] == {
            .Header -> {
                if word && token.text == "in" -> states[last] = .Pattern
            }
            .Pattern -> {
                if {
                    symbol && token.text == ")" -> {
                        if pattern != "*" -> arms += 1
                        pattern = ""
                        states[last] = .Body
                    }
                    // A leading `(` and the `&` of a `;;&` are no pattern.
                    !(symbol && pattern == "" && (token.text == "(" || (token.text == "&" && before == ";;"))) -> pattern = "{pattern}{token.text}"
                }
            }
            .Body -> {
                if symbol && (token.text == ";;" || (token.text == "&" && before == ";")) -> states[last] = .Pattern
            }
        }
    }
    arms
}

// The arms of the multi-arm Jet `if` block opened at `open` that are not
// `else`: each `->` directly inside it, outside brackets.
jet_arms: fn(list: [Token], open: Int) -> Int Never! {
    braces := 0
    brackets := 0
    arms := 0
    loop index in open..<list.len() {
        token: list[index]
        if token.kind != .Symbol -> next
        if token.text == "{{" -> braces += 1
        if token.text == "}}" {
            braces -= 1
            if braces == 0 -> return arms
        }
        if token.text == "(" || token.text == "[" -> brackets += 1
        if token.text == ")" || token.text == "]" -> brackets -= 1
        if token.text == "->" && braces == 1 && brackets == 0 {
            before: list[index - 1]
            if !(before.kind == .Word && before.text == "else") -> arms += 1
        }
    }
    arms
}

// The decisions of the Jet `if` at `at`: 1, or for a multi-arm `if {` or
// `if x == {` its arms that are not `else`.
jet_if_branches: fn(list: [Token], at: Int) -> Int Never! {
    brackets := 0
    index := at + 1
    loop {
        if index >= list.len() -> return 1
        token: list[index]
        if token.kind == .Symbol {
            if token.text == "(" || token.text == "[" -> brackets += 1
            if token.text == ")" || token.text == "]" -> brackets -= 1
            if brackets == 0 && token.text == "->" -> return 1
            if brackets == 0 && token.text == "{{" {
                before: list[index - 1]
                if index == at + 1 || (before.kind == .Symbol && before.text == "==") -> return jet_arms(list, index)
                return 1
            }
        }
        index += 1
    }
}

branches: fn(list: [Token], language: Language) -> Int Never! {
    counted: branch_words(language)
    count := if language == .Shell -> shell_arms(list) else -> 0
    loop index in 0..<list.len() {
        token: list[index]
        if token.kind == .Text -> next
        count += if counted.contains(token.text) -> 1 else -> ruled_branches(list, index, language)
    }
    count
}

// Whether the `{` at `at`, on the line whose first token is at `head`, opens
// a control block.
control_brace: fn(list: [Token], head: Int, at: Int) -> Bool Never! {
    if at > 0 {
        before: list[at - 1]
        if before.kind == .Symbol && (before.text == "->" || before.text == "??") -> return true
    }
    lead: list[head]
    if lead.kind == .Word && CONTROL_WORDS.contains(lead.text) -> return true
    if lead.kind == .Symbol && lead.text == "}}" && head + 1 < list.len() {
        after: list[head + 1]
        if after.kind == .Word && (after.text == "else" || after.text == "catch" || after.text == "finally") -> return true
    }
    false
}

// Jet and JavaScript: the most control blocks open at once.
brace_depth: fn(list: [Token]) -> Int Never! {
    open := [Bool]{}
    size := 0
    controls := 0
    deepest := 0
    head := 0
    loop index in 0..<list.len() {
        token: list[index]
        if token.first -> head = index
        if token.kind != .Symbol -> next
        if token.text == "{{" {
            control: control_brace(list, head, index)
            if size < open.len() {
                open[size] = control
            } else {
                open.push(control)
            }
            size += 1
            if control {
                controls += 1
                if controls > deepest -> deepest = controls
            }
        }
        if token.text == "}}" && size > 0 {
            size -= 1
            if open[size] -> controls -= 1
        }
    }
    deepest
}

// Python: the most control blocks open at once, from the indentation of
// each line's first token outside brackets.
python_depth: fn(list: [Token]) -> Int Never! {
    columns := [Int]{0}
    control := [Bool]{false}
    size := 1
    controls := 0
    deepest := 0
    brackets := 0
    header := ""
    loop token in list {
        if token.first && brackets == 0 {
            if token.column > columns[size - 1] {
                opened: CONTROL_WORDS.contains(header)
                if size < columns.len() {
                    columns[size] = token.column
                    control[size] = opened
                } else {
                    columns.push(token.column)
                    control.push(opened)
                }
                size += 1
                if opened {
                    controls += 1
                    if controls > deepest -> deepest = controls
                }
            } else {
                loop {
                    if size <= 1 || columns[size - 1] <= token.column -> break
                    size -= 1
                    if control[size] -> controls -= 1
                }
            }
            header = if token.kind == .Word -> token.text.copy() else -> ""
        }
        if token.kind == .Symbol {
            if token.text == "(" || token.text == "[" || token.text == "{{" -> brackets += 1
            if (token.text == ")" || token.text == "]" || token.text == "}}") && brackets > 0 -> brackets -= 1
        }
    }
    deepest
}

// Shell: the most `if`, `for`, `while`, `until` and `case` blocks open at once.
shell_depth: fn(list: [Token]) -> Int Never! {
    open := 0
    deepest := 0
    loop token in list {
        if token.kind != .Word -> next
        if SHELL_OPENERS.contains(token.text) {
            open += 1
            if open > deepest -> deepest = open
        }
        if SHELL_CLOSERS.contains(token.text) && open > 0 -> open -= 1
    }
    deepest
}

proxies: fn(list: [Token], language: Language) -> Proxies Never! {
    depth: if language == {
        .Python -> python_depth(list)
        .Shell -> shell_depth(list)
        .Jet -> brace_depth(list)
        .JavaScript -> brace_depth(list)
    }
    Proxies{branches: branches(list, language), depth: depth}
}

// ---- the review record ----

is_date: fn(text: String) -> Bool Never! {
    bytes: text.bytes()
    if bytes.len() != 10 -> return false
    loop index in 0..<10 {
        code: Int.from_u8(bytes[index])
        dash: index == 4 || index == 7
        if dash && code != 45 -> return false
        if !dash && !is_digit(code) -> return false
    }
    true
}

// The review record `text`, read, with every problem that makes it fail.
review_of: fn(text: String) -> Review Never! {
    review := Review{reviewer: "", date: "", original: 0, jet: 0, helpers_original: 0, helpers_jet: 0, problems: [String]{}}
    tree: json.parse(text) ?? {
        review.problems.push("it is not JSON: {err}")
        return review
    }
    if !is_object(tree) {
        review.problems.push("it is not a JSON object")
        return review
    }
    loop key in keys_of(tree) {
        if !REVIEW_FIELDS.contains(key) -> review.problems.push("`{key}` is not a review field")
    }
    review.reviewer = text_field(tree, "reviewer")
    if review.reviewer.trim() == "" -> review.problems.push("it names no `reviewer`")
    review.date = text_field(tree, "date")
    if !is_date(review.date) -> review.problems.push("its `date` is not YYYY-MM-DD")
    checklist: field(tree, "checklist")
    if !is_object(checklist) -> review.problems.push("it has no `checklist` object")
    loop key in keys_of(checklist) {
        if !SIDES.contains(key) -> review.problems.push("`checklist.{key}` is not `original` or `jet`")
    }
    loop side in SIDES {
        scores: field(checklist, side)
        if !is_object(scores) {
            review.problems.push("`checklist.{side}` is missing")
            next
        }
        loop key in keys_of(scores) {
            if !CHECKLIST.contains(key) -> review.problems.push("`checklist.{side}.{key}` is not a checklist item")
        }
        total := 0
        loop item in CHECKLIST {
            score: int_of(field(scores, item)) ?? -1
            if score < 0 || score > CHECKLIST_TOP {
                review.problems.push("`checklist.{side}.{item}` is missing or not a score from 0 to {CHECKLIST_TOP}")
                next
            }
            total += score
        }
        if side == "jet" -> review.jet = total else -> review.original = total
    }
    helpers: field(tree, "helpers")
    if is_null(helpers) -> return review
    if !is_object(helpers) {
        review.problems.push("`helpers` is not an object")
        return review
    }
    loop key in keys_of(helpers) {
        if !SIDES.contains(key) -> review.problems.push("`helpers.{key}` is not `original` or `jet`")
    }
    loop side in SIDES {
        listed: field(helpers, side)
        if is_null(listed) -> next
        is_list := false
        names := [Dyn]{}
        if listed == .Array(items) {
            is_list = true
            names = items.copy()
        }
        if !is_list {
            review.problems.push("`helpers.{side}` is not a list of helper names")
            next
        }
        count := 0
        loop item in names {
            name: if item == .Text(helper) -> helper.trim().copy() else -> ""
            if name == "" {
                review.problems.push("`helpers.{side}` holds a value that is not a helper name")
                next
            }
            count += 1
        }
        if side == "jet" -> review.helpers_jet = count else -> review.helpers_original = count
    }
    review
}

// The review record at `repo`/`path`, or None when there is none.
review_at: fn(repo: String, path: String) -[FS]> Review? Never! {
    if !files.is_file(files.join(repo, path)) -> return None
    text: files.read(files.join(repo, path)) ?? return Val(Review{reviewer: "", date: "", original: 0, jet: 0, helpers_original: 0, helpers_jet: 0, problems: [String]{"it cannot be read: {err}"}})
    Val(review_of(text))
}

// ---- bars ----

delta: fn(change: Int) -> String Never! {
    if change > 0 -> return "+{change}"
    "{change}"
}

// `part`/`whole` to two places, rounded half up.
ratio: fn(part: Int, whole: Int) -> String Never! {
    if whole <= 0 -> return "n/a"
    hundredths: (part * 200 + whole) /% (whole * 2)
    cents: hundredths - (hundredths /% 100) * 100
    pad: if cents < 10 -> "0" else -> ""
    "{hundredths /% 100}.{pad}{cents}"
}

// `value` in tenths of `unit`, as "12.3".
tenths: fn(value: Int, unit: Int) -> String Never! {
    scaled: (value * 10 + unit /% 2) /% unit
    "{scaled /% 10}.{scaled - (scaled /% 10) * 10}"
}

least: fn(values: [Int]) -> Int Never! {
    low := values[0]
    loop value in values {
        if value < low -> low = value
    }
    low
}

most: fn(values: [Int]) -> Int Never! {
    high := values[0]
    loop value in values {
        if value > high -> high = value
    }
    high
}

median: fn(values: [Int]) -> Int Never! {
    sorted := values.copy()
    sorted.sort()
    sorted[sorted.len() /% 2]
}

// How Jet's rounds compare with the original's: Win when every Jet round is
// below every original round, Loss for the reverse, else Even.
lead: fn(twin: [Int], original: [Int]) -> Lead Never! {
    if most(twin) < least(original) -> return Lead.Win
    if least(twin) > most(original) -> return Lead.Loss
    Lead.Even
}

lead_text: fn(result: Lead) -> String Never! {
    if result == {
        .Win -> "every Jet round below every original round"
        .Loss -> "lost: every original round below every Jet round"
        .Even -> "inconclusive: the rounds overlap"
    }
}

speed_bar: fn(wall_original: [Int], wall_jet: [Int], peak_original: [Int], peak_jet: [Int], problems: [String]) -> Bar Never! {
    if problems.len() > 0 -> return Bar{name: "speed", pass: false, detail: "not measured: {problems.join("; ")}"}
    if least(peak_original) <= 0 || least(peak_jet) <= 0 -> return Bar{name: "speed", pass: false, detail: "not measured: a run's peak memory was not recorded"}
    wall: lead(wall_jet, wall_original)
    peak: lead(peak_jet, peak_original)
    wall_text: "wall Jet/original {ratio(median(wall_jet), median(wall_original))} ({tenths(median(wall_jet), 1000000)} ms against {tenths(median(wall_original), 1000000)} ms; {lead_text(wall)})"
    peak_text: "peak memory Jet/original {ratio(median(peak_jet), median(peak_original))} ({tenths(median(peak_jet), 1048576)} MB against {tenths(median(peak_original), 1048576)} MB; {lead_text(peak)})"
    Bar{name: "speed", pass: wall == .Win && peak == .Win, detail: "{wall_text}; {peak_text}; medians of {wall_jet.len()} interleaved rounds"}
}

// The tokens bar: Jet at or below the original, or a gap `gaps` names what
// closes.
tokens_bar: fn(original: Int, twin: Int, gaps: [String], unmeasured: String) -> Bar {
    if unmeasured != "" -> return Bar{name: "tokens", pass: false, detail: unmeasured}
    counts: "Jet {twin}, original {original} ({delta(twin - original)}, Jet/original {ratio(twin, original)})"
    if {
        twin <= original -> Bar{name: "tokens", pass: true, detail: counts}
        gaps.len() > 0 -> Bar{name: "tokens", pass: true, detail: "{counts}; the gap is {gaps.join(", ")}'s"}
        else -> Bar{name: "tokens", pass: false, detail: "{counts}; the gap names no criterion or ballot (`tool.token_gaps`)"}
    }
}

// The reasoning bar from the review record at `path` (None when there is
// none) and both programs' proxies; `unmeasured` is why the proxies of the
// original could not be measured, or "".
reasoning_bar: fn(path: String, review: Review?, original: Proxies, twin: Proxies, unmeasured: String) -> Bar Never! {
    parts := [String]{}
    pass := true
    valid := false
    if review == .Val(record) {
        if record.problems.len() > 0 {
            pass = false
            parts.push("review record `{path}` fails: {record.problems.join("; ")}")
        } else {
            valid = true
            top: CHECKLIST.len() * CHECKLIST_TOP
            if record.jet < record.original -> pass = false
            parts.push("checklist Jet {record.jet}/{top}, original {record.original}/{top} ({delta(record.jet - record.original)}; {record.reviewer}, {record.date})")
            if record.helpers_jet > record.helpers_original -> pass = false
            parts.push("library-replaceable helpers Jet {record.helpers_jet}, original {record.helpers_original} ({delta(record.helpers_jet - record.helpers_original)})")
        }
    } else {
        pass = false
        parts.push("no review record `{path}`")
    }
    if unmeasured != "" {
        pass = false
        parts.push(unmeasured.copy())
    } else {
        if twin.branches > original.branches || twin.depth > original.depth -> pass = false
        parts.push("branches Jet {twin.branches}, original {original.branches} ({delta(twin.branches - original.branches)})")
        parts.push("control nesting Jet {twin.depth}, original {original.depth} ({delta(twin.depth - original.depth)})")
    }
    Bar{name: "reasoning", pass: pass && valid, detail: parts.join("; ")}
}

first_line: fn(text: String) -> String Never! { text.partition("\n").head.copy() }

// Where side `side` runs case `index` of entry `name`.
case_dir: fn(work: String, name: String, index: Int, side: Int) -> String Never! { files.join(work, "{name}/case-{index + 1}-{SIDES[side]}") }

// Judges the tool entry `name` of `repo` on every bar, running its programs
// under `work` with `jet` and `runs` timing rounds.
judge: fn(repo: String, name: String, jet: String, runs: Int, work: String) -[Env, Exec, FS, Time, Time.Wait]> Report Never! {
    entry := read_entry(repo, name)
    report := Report{entry: name.copy(), bars: [Bar]{}}
    timer: process.which("time") ?? ""
    if timer == "" -> entry.problems.push("GNU `time`, which every run goes through, is not on PATH")
    if entry.problems.len() > 0 {
        why: "the entry cannot be judged: {entry.problems.join("; ")}"
        loop bar in BARS -> report.bars.push(Bar{name: bar.copy(), pass: false, detail: why.copy()})
        return report
    }
    inherited: jet_env(jet)
    programs: [[String]]{original_command(files.join(repo, entry.original)), [String]{jet.copy(), files.join(repo, entry.twin)}}
    fixtures: if entry.fixtures == "" -> "" else -> files.join(repo, "{entry.dir}/{entry.fixtures}")
    expected := [String]{}
    loop case in entry.cases -> expected.push(files.read(files.join(repo, "{entry.dir}/{case.expected}")) ?? "")

    failures := [String]{}
    identical := 0
    loop index in 0..<entry.cases.len() {
        same := true
        loop side in 0..<2 {
            raw: run_case(programs[side], entry.cases[index], inherited, fixtures, case_dir(work, name, index, side), timer)
            check: entry.cases[index].check
            run: if check == "" -> raw else -> checked(raw, files.join(repo, "{entry.dir}/{check}"), jet, entry.cases[index], inherited, case_dir(work, name, index, side))
            why: run_failure(run, entry.cases[index], expected[index])
            if why != "" {
                same = false
                failures.push("case {index + 1} {SIDES[side]}: {why}")
            }
        }
        if same -> identical += 1
    }
    cases: entry.cases.len()
    parity_detail: if failures.len() == 0 -> "{cases}/{cases} cases do the job" else -> "{identical}/{cases} cases do the job; {failures.join("; ")}"
    report.bars.push(Bar{name: "parity", pass: failures.len() == 0, detail: parity_detail})

    wall_original := [Int]{}
    wall_jet := [Int]{}
    peak_original := [Int]{}
    peak_jet := [Int]{}
    problems := [String]{}
    loop round in 0..<runs {
        loop step in 0..<2 {
            side: if (round /% 2) * 2 == round -> step else -> 1 - step
            wall := 0
            peak := 0
            loop index in 0..<cases {
                run: run_case(programs[side], entry.cases[index], inherited, fixtures, case_dir(work, name, index, side), timer)
                if run.problem != "" && problems.len() == 0 -> problems.push("case {index + 1} {SIDES[side]}: {run.problem}")
                wall += run.wall_ns
                if run.peak_bytes > peak -> peak = run.peak_bytes
            }
            if side == 0 {
                wall_original.push(wall)
                peak_original.push(peak)
            } else {
                wall_jet.push(wall)
                peak_jet.push(peak)
            }
        }
    }
    report.bars.push(speed_bar(wall_original, wall_jet, peak_original, peak_jet, problems))

    original_text: files.read(files.join(repo, entry.original)) ?? ""
    language: language_of(entry.original, first_line(original_text))
    unmeasured: if language == None -> "no token or proxy rule for the original `{entry.original}`'s language" else -> ""
    original: program(repo, entry.original, language ?? .Shell)
    twin: program(repo, entry.twin, .Jet)
    record: "{entry.dir}/{REVIEW_FILE}"
    report.bars.push(reasoning_bar(record, review_at(repo, record), proxies(original.tokens, language ?? .Shell), proxies(twin.tokens, .Jet), unmeasured))
    report.bars.push(tokens_bar(original.tokens.len(), twin.tokens.len(), entry.token_gaps, unmeasured))
    report
}

// The `--measure` rows of entry `name`: for each side its tokens, branches,
// control nesting depth and files (SOURCE RULES), without running a case.
measure_lines: fn(repo: String, name: String) -[FS]> [String] Never! {
    entry: read_entry(repo, name)
    if entry.problems.len() > 0 -> return [String]{"{name}\t-\t-\t-\t-\tcannot be measured: {entry.problems.join("; ")}"}
    original_text: files.read(files.join(repo, entry.original)) ?? ""
    language: language_of(entry.original, first_line(original_text)) ?? return [String]{"{name}\t-\t-\t-\t-\tno token or proxy rule for the original `{entry.original}`'s language"}
    sides: [Program]{program(repo, entry.original, language), program(repo, entry.twin, .Jet)}
    languages: [Language]{language, .Jet}
    out := [String]{}
    loop side in 0..<2 {
        measured: proxies(sides[side].tokens, languages[side])
        out.push("{name}\t{SIDES[side]}\t{sides[side].tokens.len()}\t{measured.branches}\t{measured.depth}\t{program_files(sides[side])}")
    }
    out
}

// The bars `report` loses, by name.
lost_bars: fn(report: Report) -> [String] Never! {
    out := [String]{}
    loop bar in report.bars {
        if !bar.pass -> out.push(bar.name.copy())
    }
    out
}

// The rows of `report`: one per bar, then the verdict.
report_lines: fn(report: Report) -> [String] Never! {
    out := [String]{}
    loop bar in report.bars {
        result: if bar.pass -> "PASS" else -> "FAIL"
        out.push("{report.entry}\t{bar.name}\t{result}\t{bar.detail}")
    }
    lost: lost_bars(report)
    if {
        lost.len() == 0 -> out.push("{report.entry}\tverdict\tPASS\twins every bar; the repository may switch to the Jet twin")
        else -> out.push("{report.entry}\tverdict\tFAIL\tloses {lost.join(", ")}; the original keeps running")
    }
    out
}

// `path` from the working directory when it is relative.
absolute: fn(path: String) -[Env, FS]> String Never! {
    if path.starts_with("/") -> return path.copy()
    files.join(files.cwd() ?? ".", path)
}

// The checkout holding this tool, else the working directory.
repo_root: fn() -[Env, FS]> String Never! {
    tool: "/Tools/gauntlet/PortBars.jet"
    script: absolute(sys.executable())
    if script.ends_with(tool) -> return script.removesuffix(tool)
    files.cwd() ?? "."
}

// The scratch root (Tools/agent/roots.sh): $JET_SCRATCH_ROOT, else
// $JET_STATE_ROOT, else Jet's user cache. Work directories stay there, on
// disk: on a RAM-backed /tmp a killed judge's leftovers hold memory.
scratch_root: fn() -[Env]> String Never! {
    cache: process.env_get("XDG_CACHE_HOME") ?? "{process.env_get("HOME") ?? ""}/.cache"
    process.env_get("JET_SCRATCH_ROOT") ?? process.env_get("JET_STATE_ROOT") ?? "{cache}/jet-dev"
}

// A fresh work directory `port_bars_<label>_<pid>_<ns>` under the scratch
// root. First it removes the `port_bars_*` directories that killed judges left
// there or in the temporary directory, where earlier judges made theirs: each
// one whose pid (the name's second-to-last field) has no /proc entry.
work_dir: fn(label: String) -[Env, FS, Time]> String IOError! {
    root: scratch_root()
    loop dir in [root, files.gettempdir()] {
        entries: files.list_dir(dir, matching: "port_bars_*") ?? next
        loop entry in entries {
            fields: entry.name.split("_").to_list()
            pid: fields[fields.len() - 2].to_int() ?? next
            if entry.is_dir && !files.exists("/proc/{pid}") -> files.remove_all(files.join(dir, entry.name)) ?? ()
        }
    }
    work: files.join(root, "port_bars_{label}_{sys.pid()}_{time.unix_ns()}")
    files.create_dir_all(work) ?? return Err(err)
    Ok(work)
}

cannot_run: fn(message: String) -[Exec, IO]> Never { process.fail(64, message) }

usage: fn() -[Exec, IO]> Never { cannot_run("usage: jet Tools/gauntlet/PortBars.jet [--entry NAME] [--runs N] [--jet PATH] [--repo DIR] [--measure]") }

run: fn() {
    args: process.args()
    repo := repo_root()
    only := ""
    runs := DEFAULT_RUNS
    jet := process.env_get("JET") ?? "jet"
    measure := false
    index := 0
    loop {
        if index >= args.len() -> break
        if args[index] == "--measure" {
            measure = true
            index += 1
            next
        }
        if index + 1 >= args.len() -> usage()
        value: args[index + 1]
        if {
            args[index] == "--entry" -> only = value.copy()
            args[index] == "--runs" -> runs = value.to_int() ?? usage()
            args[index] == "--jet" -> jet = value.copy()
            args[index] == "--repo" -> repo = absolute(value)
            else -> usage()
        }
        index += 2
    }
    if runs < 1 -> usage()
    if jet.contains("/") -> jet = absolute(jet)
    names := [String]{}
    if only != "" {
        if !files.is_file(files.join(repo, "{ENTRIES_ROOT}/{only}/entry.json")) -> cannot_run("port-bars: there is no entry `{ENTRIES_ROOT}/{only}`")
        names.push(only.copy())
    } else {
        names = tool_entries(repo) ?? return cannot_run(err.message)
    }
    if measure {
        print("entry\tside\ttokens\tbranches\tdepth\tfiles")
        loop name in names {
            loop line in measure_lines(repo, name) -> print(line)
        }
        return
    }
    work: work_dir("judge") ?? return cannot_run("port-bars: a scratch directory cannot be made: {err}")
    failed := 0
    print("entry\tbar\tresult\tdetail")
    loop name in names {
        report: judge(repo, name, jet, runs, work)
        loop line in report_lines(report) -> print(line)
        if lost_bars(report).len() > 0 -> failed += 1
    }
    files.remove_all(work) ?? ()
    print("port bars: {names.len()} entries, {names.len() - failed} pass, {failed} fail")
    if failed > 0 -> process.exit(1)
}

// ---- tests ----

#Test("a program's tokens and proxies span the repository modules it imports, transitively and once each, on both sides") {
    dir: work_dir("sources") ?? panic("a scratch directory cannot be made: {err}")
    plant(dir, "Tools/fx/a.mjs", "import fs from 'node:fs';\nimport {{ b }} from './b.mjs';\nimport {{\n  c,\n}} from \"../fy/c.mjs\";\nimport '../../../outside.mjs';\nif (b) c();\n")
    plant(dir, "Tools/fx/b.mjs", "import {{ c }} from '../fy/c.mjs';\nexport const b = 1;\n")
    plant(dir, "Tools/fy/c.mjs", "import {{ b }} from '../fx/b.mjs';\nexport function c() {{ if (b) return 2; }}\n")
    plant(dir, "Tools/fx/run.sh", "#!/bin/sh\n. \"$(dirname \"$0\")/../roots.sh\"\necho ok\n")
    plant(dir, "Tools/roots.sh", "if true; then root=x; fi\n")
    plant(dir, "Tools/fx/Twin.jet", "use {{\n    files: core.files\n    helper: \"Helper\"\n}}\nuse header: \"counter.h\"\nrun: fn() {{ print(helper.two()) }}\n")
    plant(dir, "Tools/fx/Helper.jet", "two: fn() -> Int {{ if true -> 2 else -> 1 }}\n#Test(\"two\") {{ assert(two() == 2) }}\n")
    plant(dir, "Tools/fx/pkg/tool.py", "from .util import go\nfrom . import extra\ngo()\n")
    plant(dir, "Tools/fx/pkg/util.py", "def go():\n    if True:\n        pass\n")
    plant(dir, "Tools/fx/pkg/extra.py", "x = 1\n")
    javascript: program(dir, "Tools/fx/a.mjs", .JavaScript)
    assert_eq(javascript.paths, ["Tools/fx/a.mjs", "Tools/fx/b.mjs", "Tools/fy/c.mjs"])
    each := 0
    loop path in javascript.paths -> each += tokens(files.read(files.join(dir, path)) ?? "", .JavaScript).len()
    assert_eq(javascript.tokens.len(), each)
    assert_eq(javascript.counts.len(), 3)
    assert_eq(proxies(javascript.tokens, .JavaScript), Proxies{branches: 2, depth: 0})
    shell: program(dir, "Tools/fx/run.sh", .Shell)
    assert_eq(shell.paths, ["Tools/fx/run.sh", "Tools/roots.sh"])
    assert_eq(proxies(shell.tokens, .Shell), Proxies{branches: 1, depth: 1})
    twin: program(dir, "Tools/fx/Twin.jet", .Jet)
    assert_eq(twin.paths, ["Tools/fx/Twin.jet", "Tools/fx/Helper.jet"])
    assert_eq(twin.counts[1], without_tests(tokens(files.read(files.join(dir, "Tools/fx/Helper.jet")) ?? "", .Jet)).len())
    assert_eq(proxies(twin.tokens, .Jet), Proxies{branches: 1, depth: 0})
    python: program(dir, "Tools/fx/pkg/tool.py", .Python)
    assert_eq(python.paths, ["Tools/fx/pkg/tool.py", "Tools/fx/pkg/util.py", "Tools/fx/pkg/extra.py"])
    assert_eq(normalized("Tools/fx/../../../x.mjs"), "")
    files.remove_all(dir) ?? ()
}

#Test("a Jet twin counts the package sources it takes names from, those they use, and their package's own dependencies") {
    dir: work_dir("package") ?? panic("a scratch directory cannot be made: {err}")
    plant(dir, "Tools/base/package.jet", "name: \"base\"\nversion: \"0.0.1\"\n")
    plant(dir, "Tools/base/Source/D.jet", "delta: fn() -> Int {{ 4 }}\n")
    plant(dir, "Tools/base/Source/E.jet", "epsilon: fn() -> Int {{ 5 }}\n")
    plant(dir, "Tools/kit/package.jet", "name: \"kit\"\nversion: \"0.0.1\"\ndeps: {{\n    base: ../base,\n}}\n")
    plant(dir, "Tools/kit/Source/A.jet", "use base.[delta]\n\nalpha: fn() -> Int {{ beta() + delta() }}\n")
    plant(dir, "Tools/kit/Source/B.jet", "beta: fn() -> Int {{ 2 }}\n")
    plant(dir, "Tools/kit/Source/C.jet", "gamma: fn() -> Int {{ 3 }}\n")
    plant(dir, "Tools/fx/twin/run.jet", "package: {{\n    name: \"twin\"\n    version: \"0.0.1\"\n    deps: {{\n        kit: ../../kit,\n    }}\n}}\n\nuse {{\n    kit.[alpha]\n    math: core.math\n}}\n\nrun: fn() {{ print(alpha()) }}\n")
    twin: program(dir, "Tools/fx/twin/run.jet", .Jet)
    assert_eq(twin.paths, ["Tools/fx/twin/run.jet", "Tools/kit/Source/A.jet", "Tools/kit/Source/B.jet", "Tools/base/Source/D.jet"])
    assert_eq(package_names("use {{\n    kit.[alpha, beta]\n    one: kit.gamma\n}}\nuse kit.delta\n", "kit"), ["alpha", "beta", "gamma", "delta"])
    files.remove_all(dir) ?? ()
}

#Test("a work directory is made under the scratch root, after a dead judge's leftover there is removed") {
    root: scratch_root()
    // No process has pid 999999999: Linux's pid_max is at most 4194304.
    stale: files.join(root, "port_bars_judge_999999999_1")
    files.create_dir_all(stale) ?? panic("`{stale}` cannot be made: {err}")
    work: work_dir("sweep") ?? panic("a scratch directory cannot be made: {err}")
    assert(work.starts_with(files.join(root, "port_bars_sweep_{sys.pid()}_")))
    assert(files.is_dir(work))
    assert(!files.exists(stale))
    files.remove_all(work) ?? ()
}

#Test("each language's token rule counts words, symbols and whole strings, never comments or the #! line") {
    assert_eq(tokens("run: fn() {{ print(\"{{a.join(\", \")}} done\") }} // note\n", .Jet).len(), 11)
    assert_eq(without_tests(tokens("run: fn() {{ print(1) }}\n#Test(\"one (\") {{\n    if f(1) == 1 {{ assert(true) }}\n}}\n", .Jet)).len(), 11)
    assert_eq(tokens("#!/usr/bin/env node\nconst a = `x ${{b + \"}}\"}} y`; /* c */ if (a === 'q') f(a) // d\n", .JavaScript).len(), 15)
    assert_eq(tokens("x = a / 2; y = s.replace(/(?<!['\"])\\/x[/]/g, '');\nz = /a?b/.test(s) ? 1 : 0\n", .JavaScript).len(), 29)
    assert_eq(tokens("x = f'{{y}}' # c\nif x and y:\n    print(r\"a\\\\b\")\n", .Python).len(), 12)
    assert_eq(tokens("#!/bin/sh\n# c\nx=\"$HOME/#\" # d\necho ${{x#a}} $# 'q'\n", .Shell).len(), 8)
    assert(language_of("Tools/x/run", "#!/usr/bin/env -S python3 -u") == Val(Language.Python))
    assert(language_of("Tools/x/run.sh", "") == Val(Language.Shell))
    assert(language_of("Tools/x/run", "plain") == None)
}

#Test("a JavaScript regex literal is one token, and a backtick or slash inside it opens nothing") {
    // run-cold-context.mjs:239's pattern holds three backticks (#5072 c54).
    source: "const r = /(?:^|\\s)(\\d+)\\.\\s+`([^`]+)`/gm;\nconst q = a / b / c;\nif (/[/`]/.test(s)) f(`t`)\nreturn /x/i\n"
    list: tokens(source, .JavaScript)
    assert_eq(list.len(), 29)
    assert(list[3].kind == .Text)
    assert_eq(list[9].text, "/")
    assert(list[16].kind == .Text)
    assert(list[28].kind == .Text)
}

#Test("the Jet decision table counts if (or a multi-arm if's arms but else), loop, &&, || and ??, and the deepest control nesting") {
    jet: "check: fn(a: Int) -> Int {{\n    if a == {{\n        1 -> return 1\n        2 -> {{\n            loop i in 0..<a {{\n                if i > 0 && a > 1 -> return i\n            }}\n        }}\n        else -> return 0\n    }}\n    a ?? 0\n}}\n"
    assert_eq(proxies(tokens(jet, .Jet), .Jet), Proxies{branches: 6, depth: 3})
    arms: "f: fn(a: Int?) -> Int {{\n    b: if {{\n        a == None -> 0\n        else -> 1\n    }}\n    if b > 0 || false -> b else -> a ?? 2\n}}\n"
    assert_eq(branches(tokens(arms, .Jet), .Jet), 4)
}

#Test("the JavaScript decision table counts if, ?, case but default, for, while, &&, ||, ??, ?. and catch, never inside a regex literal") {
    javascript: "function f(x) {{\n  if (x) {{\n    for (const a of x) {{\n      g(a ? 1 : 2);\n    }}\n  }} else {{\n    try {{ h(); }} catch (e) {{ return x ?? 0; }}\n  }}\n}}\n"
    assert_eq(proxies(tokens(javascript, .JavaScript), .JavaScript), Proxies{branches: 5, depth: 2})
    fallbacks: "const a = o?.b ?? c;\nswitch (k) {{\n  case 1: f(); break;\n  default: g();\n}}\nconst r = /x?y|z/;\nwhile (a && !b || c) h();\n"
    assert_eq(branches(tokens(fallbacks, .JavaScript), .JavaScript), 6)
}

#Test("the Python decision table counts if, elif, case but case _, for, while, and, or and except") {
    python: "def f(x):\n    for a in x:\n        if a:\n            try:\n                g(a)\n            except E:\n                pass\n    return [b for b in x if b or a]\n"
    assert_eq(proxies(tokens(python, .Python), .Python), Proxies{branches: 6, depth: 3})
    arms: "match k:\n    case 1:\n        pass\n    case _:\n        pass\nwhile a and b:\n    pass\nif a:\n    pass\nelif b:\n    pass\nx = y if z else w\n"
    assert_eq(branches(tokens(arms, .Python), .Python), 6)
}

#Test("the shell decision table counts if, elif, each case arm but *), for, while, until, &&, || and each ${{x:-…}} fallback") {
    shell: "f() {{\n  if [ -n \"$1\" ] && true; then\n    for a in b; do\n      case $a in\n        x) echo 1 ;;\n        *) echo 2 ;;\n      esac\n    done\n  fi\n}}\n"
    assert_eq(proxies(tokens(shell, .Shell), .Shell), Proxies{branches: 4, depth: 3})
    arms: "case $1 in\n  a|b) x=${{2:-none}} ;;\n  (c) y=${{3:+set}}\nesac\nuntil false || ${{#z}}; do w=${{v:2}} ${{u%x}} ${{q=${{r?}}}}; done\nif a; then :; elif b; then :; fi\n"
    assert_eq(proxies(tokens(arms, .Shell), .Shell), Proxies{branches: 10, depth: 1})
}

// "TOKENS BRANCHES" of `source` read as `language`.
counted: fn(source: String, language: Language) -> String Never! {
    list: tokens(source, language)
    "{list.len()} {branches(list, language)}"
}

#Test("a JavaScript slash divides after an operand, a postfix ++ or --, a call's or group's closing paren and an object's closing brace, and opens a regex literal after a keyword, an operator, a control head's closing paren and a block's closing brace") {
    assert_eq(counted("x++ / 2; if (y) f();", .JavaScript), "14 1")
    assert_eq(counted("if (x) /a?b/.test(y);", .JavaScript), "11 1")
    assert_eq(counted("x-- / 2 ? a : b;", .JavaScript), "10 1")
    assert_eq(counted("a = b / c / d ? e : f;", .JavaScript), "12 1")
    assert_eq(counted("g(x) / 2 ? a : b;", .JavaScript), "11 1")
    assert_eq(counted("(a) / 2 ? b : c;", .JavaScript), "10 1")
    assert_eq(counted("v[0] / 2 ? a : b;", .JavaScript), "11 1")
    assert_eq(counted("const o = {{}} / 2 ? a : b;", .JavaScript), "12 1")
    assert_eq(counted("while (x) /a?/.exec(s);", .JavaScript), "11 1")
    assert_eq(counted("for (;;) /a?|b/.test(s);", .JavaScript), "11 1")
    assert_eq(counted("for await (const l of r) /a?/.test(l);", .JavaScript), "15 1")
    assert_eq(counted("if (x) {{}} /a?b/.test(y);", .JavaScript), "13 1")
    assert_eq(counted("function f() {{}} /a?/.test(s);", .JavaScript), "13 0")
    assert_eq(counted("return /a?/.test(s) ? 1 : 2;", .JavaScript), "12 1")
    assert_eq(counted("typeof /a?/;", .JavaScript), "3 0")
    assert_eq(counted("x = y ? /a?/ : z;", .JavaScript), "8 1")
}

#Test("a shell case arm ends at each of ;;, ;& and ;;&, and the default *) after any of them counts none") {
    assert_eq(counted("case x in a) f;& b) g;; esac", .Shell), "13 2")
    assert_eq(counted("case x in a) f;;& *) g;; esac", .Shell), "13 1")
    assert_eq(counted("case x in a) f;& *) g;; esac", .Shell), "13 1")
    assert_eq(counted("case x in a) f;; b) g;;& c) h;& *) i;; esac", .Shell), "22 3")
    assert_eq(counted("case x in a) f & ;; b) g;; esac", .Shell), "13 2")
    assert_eq(counted("case x in a) f; ;; b) g; esac", .Shell), "13 2")
    assert_eq(counted("case x in a) case y in b) f;& *) g;; esac;; *) h;; esac", .Shell), "24 2")
}

// A checklist object scoring every item `score`.
review_scores: fn(score: Int) -> String Never! {
    items := [String]{}
    loop item in CHECKLIST -> items.push("\"{item}\": {score}")
    open: "{{"
    close: "}}"
    "{open}{items.join(", ")}{close}"
}

// A review record scoring every checklist item `original` and `twin`.
review_json: fn(original: Int, twin: Int, extra: String) -> String Never! {
    open: "{{"
    close: "}}"
    "{open}\"reviewer\": \"planted\", \"date\": \"2026-11-10\", \"checklist\": {open}\"original\": {review_scores(original)}, \"jet\": {review_scores(twin)}{extra}{close}{close}\n"
}

#Test("a review record fails on an unknown or missing checklist item, a bad score or an unknown field") {
    good: review_of(review_json(1, 2, ""))
    assert_eq(good.problems, [String]{})
    assert_eq(good.original, 6)
    assert_eq(good.jet, 12)
    unknown: review_of(review_json(1, 2, ", \"jet_extra\": 1").replace("\"effects_visible\": 2", "\"effects_shown\": 2"))
    assert_eq(unknown.problems, [String]{"`checklist.jet_extra` is not `original` or `jet`", "`checklist.jet.effects_shown` is not a checklist item", "`checklist.jet.effects_visible` is missing or not a score from 0 to 2"})
    bad: review_of("{{\"reviewer\": \"\", \"date\": \"11/10\", \"score\": 3, \"checklist\": {{}}, \"helpers\": {{\"jet\": [\"a\", 1]}}}}")
    assert_eq(bad.problems.len(), 6)
    assert(bad.problems.contains("`score` is not a review field"))
    assert(bad.problems.contains("`helpers.jet` holds a value that is not a helper name"))
}

#Test("the reasoning bar fails without a record and on any proxy Jet makes worse, naming the delta") {
    even: Proxies{branches: 3, depth: 2}
    record: review_of(review_json(1, 2, ""))
    assert(reasoning_bar("r.json", Val(record), even, even, "").pass)
    missing: reasoning_bar("r.json", None, even, even, "")
    assert(!missing.pass && missing.detail.starts_with("no review record `r.json`"))
    worse: reasoning_bar("r.json", Val(record), even, Proxies{branches: 4, depth: 2}, "")
    assert(!worse.pass && worse.detail.contains("branches Jet 4, original 3 (+1)"))
    lower: reasoning_bar("r.json", Val(review_of(review_json(2, 1, ""))), even, even, "")
    assert(!lower.pass && lower.detail.contains("checklist Jet 6/12, original 12/12 (-6"))
}

plant: fn(dir: String, path: String, text: String) -[FS]> () {
    files.create_dir_all(files.dirname(files.join(dir, path))) ?? panic("{path}: {err}")
    files.write(files.join(dir, path), text) ?? panic("{path}: {err}")
}

// Plants tool entry `name` pairing `original` with `twin` on one case that
// must print "3", or whose `check` must; `gaps` is its `tool.token_gaps`.
plant_entry: fn(dir: String, name: String, original: String, twin: String, review: String, check: String{""}, gaps: String{"[]"}) -[FS]> () {
    checked: if check == "" -> "" else -> ", \"check\": \"check.jet\""
    plant(dir, "{ENTRIES_ROOT}/{name}/entry.json", "{{\"name\": \"{name}\", \"mode\": \"tool\", \"tool\": {{\"original\": \"{original}\", \"jet\": \"{twin}\", \"token_gaps\": {gaps}, \"cases\": [{{\"args\": [], \"expected\": \"expected/three.out\"{checked}}}]}}}}\n")
    plant(dir, "{ENTRIES_ROOT}/{name}/expected/three.out", "3\n")
    if check != "" -> plant(dir, "{ENTRIES_ROOT}/{name}/check.jet", check)
    if review != "" -> plant(dir, "{ENTRIES_ROOT}/{name}/{REVIEW_FILE}", review)
}

#Test("a planted entry that wins every bar passes, as do a named token gap and a job its check proves, and each planted loss fails its bar alone") {
    dir: work_dir("planted") ?? panic("a scratch directory cannot be made: {err}")
    // Slow and large: half a gigabyte held for a second, a margin a warmed
    // Jet run on a loaded machine stays inside.
    plant(dir, "Tools/fx/heavy.py", "import time\nd = b\"x\" * 536870912\ntime.sleep(1)\nprint(3)\n")
    plant(dir, "Tools/fx/wrong.py", "import time\nd = b\"x\" * 536870912\ntime.sleep(1)\nprint(4)\n")
    plant(dir, "Tools/fx/fast.sh", "a=1\nb=2\nc=3\nd=4\ne=5\necho 3\n")
    plant(dir, "Tools/fx/Small.jet", "run: fn() {{ print(3) }}\n")
    plant(dir, "Tools/fx/Big.jet", "run: fn() {{\n    first: 1\n    second: 2\n    third: first + second\n    print(third)\n}}\n")
    // The same job, a file holding 3, reported in other words; and a wrong job.
    plant(dir, "Tools/fx/job.py", "import time\nd = b\"x\" * 536870912\ntime.sleep(1)\nopen(\"job\", \"w\").write(\"3\\n\")\nprint(\"python wrote the job\")\n")
    plant(dir, "Tools/fx/Job.jet", "use {{\n    files: core.files\n}}\n\nrun: fn() {{\n    files.write(\"job\", \"3\\n\")\n    print(\"done\")\n}}\n")
    plant(dir, "Tools/fx/WrongJob.jet", "use {{\n    files: core.files\n}}\n\nrun: fn() {{\n    files.write(\"job\", \"4\\n\")\n    print(\"python wrote the job\")\n}}\n")
    check: "use {{\n    files: core.files\n}}\n\nrun: fn() {{ print(files.read(\"job\").trim()) }}\n"
    review: review_json(1, 2, "")
    plant_entry(dir, "pass", "Tools/fx/heavy.py", "Tools/fx/Small.jet", review)
    plant_entry(dir, "parity", "Tools/fx/wrong.py", "Tools/fx/Small.jet", review)
    plant_entry(dir, "speed", "Tools/fx/fast.sh", "Tools/fx/Small.jet", review)
    plant_entry(dir, "tokens", "Tools/fx/heavy.py", "Tools/fx/Big.jet", review)
    plant_entry(dir, "reasoning", "Tools/fx/heavy.py", "Tools/fx/Small.jet", "")
    plant_entry(dir, "gapped", "Tools/fx/heavy.py", "Tools/fx/Big.jet", review, gaps: "[\"#5072 c36\"]")
    plant_entry(dir, "job", "Tools/fx/job.py", "Tools/fx/Job.jet", review, check: check, gaps: "[\"D-SH-RUN1\"]")
    plant_entry(dir, "wrongjob", "Tools/fx/job.py", "Tools/fx/WrongJob.jet", review, check: check, gaps: "[\"D-SH-RUN1\"]")
    jet: absolute(process.env_get("JET") ?? "jet")
    work: work_dir("work") ?? panic("a scratch directory cannot be made: {err}")
    expected: [[], ["parity"], ["speed"], ["tokens"], ["reasoning"], [], [], ["parity"]]
    names: ["pass", "parity", "speed", "tokens", "reasoning", "gapped", "job", "wrongjob"]
    loop index in 0..<names.len() {
        report: judge(dir, names[index], jet, 3, work)
        if lost_bars(report) != expected[index] {
            loop line in report_lines(report) -> print(line)
        }
        assert_eq(lost_bars(report), expected[index])
    }
    assert_eq(tool_entries(dir) ?? panic(err.message), ["gapped", "job", "parity", "pass", "reasoning", "speed", "tokens", "wrongjob"])
    plant_entry(dir, "badgap", "Tools/fx/heavy.py", "Tools/fx/Big.jet", review, gaps: "[\"soon\"]")
    assert(read_entry(dir, "badgap").problems.any(problem -> problem.contains("not a criterion")))
    files.remove_all(dir) ?? ()
    files.remove_all(work) ?? ()
}
